# MAP.md and BACKLOG_OPEN.md are fully GENERATED (scripts/build-map.mjs / build-backlog-index.mjs)
# and are regenerated on nearly every PR, so they conflict by construction on a busy day (NEW-1).
#
# ⛔ B1102688 (2026-09-03) — THE LINES BELOW USED TO NAME `merge=planyr-ledger` DIRECTLY. That name
# is a CUSTOM driver: git refuses to let `.gitattributes` carry the actual command (`merge.<name>
# .driver` is local-only config — a repo cannot be allowed to make an arbitrary clone execute an
# arbitrary command with zero action from whoever is cloning it), so a clone that has never run
# `npm install` — every fresh agent container, every fresh CI checkout — silently fell back to an
# ORDINARY 3-way text merge, with no warning at all. Both files are wholly rewritten on nearly
# every regeneration, so that fallback conflicts by construction. Measured cost the night this was
# fixed: two real PRs sat with `mergeable_state: dirty`, GitHub withholding every required check
# ("Expected — waiting for status to be reported") indefinitely — reading exactly like a CI outage.
#
# THE FIX, two layers:
#   1. The line below now names git's own BUILT-IN `union` driver (gitattributes(5) — no local
#      config, works in a bare fresh clone; proved in test/freshCloneMerge.test.js). Since both
#      files are wholly DERIVED from other inputs, a union merge can never be wrong in a way that
#      matters: whatever it leaves is corrected the instant the real generator runs again, which
#      `scripts/post-merge-regen.mjs` (the `.githooks/post-merge` hook) already does after every
#      merge, unconditionally, regardless of which driver produced the merged content.
#   2. `npm install` (or `npm run hooks:install`) UPGRADES this invisibly: `scripts/install-hooks.
#      mjs` writes a LOCAL, uncommitted `.git/info/attributes` override pointing these same two
#      paths at the smarter custom driver instead (`merge=planyr-ledger` — inline regeneration
#      during the merge itself, the B384432 hand-authored-description safety check, and the
#      ability to leave a REAL conflict for a human if regeneration fails outright, which the
#      built-in `union` default can never do). `.git/info/attributes` takes precedence over this
#      file for exactly the same reason `merge.<name>.driver` is local-only: it is per-clone,
#      uncommitted config, so writing to it needs no different trust boundary than the merge
#      driver command this repo already relies on installers to wire up.
#
# So: no install → safe, zero-config `union` (this file, alone, is sufficient — no conflict is
# ever shown). Installed → the exact same smart behavior this repo already had, unchanged, proven
# by test/mergeDriverE2E.test.js. See scripts/install-hooks.mjs for the override-writing code.
MAP.md merge=union
BACKLOG_OPEN.md merge=union

# docs/archive/BACKLOG-DONE.md is hand-authored, APPEND-ONLY history (never derived from anything,
# unlike the pair above), so it gets git's zero-config `union` driver directly — no local-override
# upgrade exists or is planned for it. Two branches each ARCHIVING a different newly-shipped item
# (the overwhelming majority of its conflicts, and the only kind git ever showed a raw conflict for
# before this fix) union safely: both entries land, nothing is lost, no config needed anywhere.
# The one case union cannot get right — two branches editing the exact SAME already-closed entry,
# rather than each adding a new one — is rare for a file nothing acts on further, and is caught
# LOUDLY rather than silently: `test/idUniqueness.test.js`'s cross-file collision guard scans this
# file's B#/V# headings and fails the build on any duplicate, naming the id. That is a materially
# different, and better, failure mode than the raw conflict this replaces: before, GitHub withheld
# every required check indefinitely with no clear cause; now, the PR merges and either passes, or
# fails on a specific, named, fixable line.
#
# BACKLOG.md / VERIFICATION.md / docs/archive/VERIFICATION-DONE.md deliberately stay OFF this —
# see scripts/resolve-ledgers.mjs's header for why a silent duplicate is a correctness failure in
# the file that is the single source of truth for what is still OPEN, in a way it is not for
# already-closed history. Do not widen this file to cover them without re-reading that reasoning.
docs/archive/BACKLOG-DONE.md merge=union
